n-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Health officials are investigating whether Ebola patients in Kenya and Nigeria crossed paths at Uganda's main airport as conflicting accounts cloud the source of one infection.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Gadi Eisenkot campaigns on Moroccan roots in challenge to Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b70b4fde068229e7ba35461f8e3d543a0c8c13fde3a1932dd703b5168fca2a7</id><updated>2026-10-25T19:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T09:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gadi-eisenkot-campaigns-on-moroccan-roots-in-challenge-to-netanyahu/a-79747193--b8bf9b894fd4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gadi-eisenkot-campaigns-on-moroccan-roots-in-challenge-to-netanyahu/a-79747193?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Israel prepares to vote, Gadi Eisenkot is leveraging his Moroccan heritage in Likud strongholds such as Sderot. From historical divides to October 7, identity and trauma are redefining the city's political loyalties.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Prague honours Roma resistance fighters against Hitler</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6723fdf97545c3750e42904cbf5fa62cbe20d7520f7b8a567c5dff84319cf02</id><updated>2026-10-25T19:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T09:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/prague-honours-roma-resistance-fighters-against-hitler/a-79725015--ffcc49569b60.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/prague-honours-roma-resistance-fighters-against-hitler/a-79725015?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than 1,400 Roma fought against the German Nazi occupation in Czechoslovakia. A new exhibition in Prague showcases the stories of partisans and soldiers whose fates barely received any attention for decades.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia looks to US for an AI edge as Yemen's Houthis up pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c3b63e8129967d331c96548cb95b63f6640684a53bc7cd3afd8bc66f0b0f3e6</id><updated>2026-10-25T19:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T09:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-looks-to-us-for-an-ai-edge-as-yemen-s-houthis-up-pressure/a-79735138--9b8ebc9e4129.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-looks-to-us-for-an-ai-edge-as-yemen-s-houthis-up-pressure/a-79735138?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US is helping Saudi Arabia fight the Houthi group in Yemen with AI-assisted targeting. But AI is not a magic bullet, experts say, and there are technological, political and human rights issues to consider.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria holds presidential elections amid divisions over Ukraine war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3381034115d98df9775709b172e4590144d52bfdf2d5a8108c6bde715ebdc699</id><updated>2026-10-25T19:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T07:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-holds-presidential-elections-amid-divisions-over-ukraine-war/a-79753496--1dfd3e71b9ce.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-holds-presidential-elections-amid-divisions-over-ukraine-war/a-79753496?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bulgarians are voting in presidential elections amid security concerns over attacks on ships in the Black Sea. The vote for the largely ceremonial post is seen as a test of the popularity of Prime Minister Rumen Radev.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey's new deal on Mediterranean maritime boundaries with Libya is exacerbating issues with Greece and the EU</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ba291ba26dae83e629db794daa7e0815dd126e44363dae8c41bfc35cdbdd07a</id><updated>2026-10-25T19:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T14:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-new-deal-on-mediterranean-maritime-boundaries-with-libya-is-exacerbating-issues-with-greece/a-79745971--8e4f859a6229.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-new-deal-on-mediterranean-maritime-boundaries-with-libya-is-exacerbating-issues-with-greece-and-the-eu/a-79745971?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Turkey and Libya plan to redraw maritime boundaries in the Mediterranean as part of a new economic corridor. This has sparked strong protests from Greece, and has also drawn the European Union into the conflict.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why Russia's arrest of Japanese journalist is the latest sign of deteriorating ties between the countries.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88f37a7e30cdb4eb518fae9d961d8ec76d70940ac81bbc116ecc714da7976e45</id><updated>2026-10-25T19:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T05:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-russia-s-arrest-of-japanese-journalist-is-the-latest-sign-of-deteriorating-ties-between-the-coun/a-79742995--e6439f04b25d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-russia-s-arrest-of-japanese-journalist-is-the-latest-sign-of-deteriorating-ties-between-the-countries/a-79742995?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Japan is demanding access to a journalist who was arrested by Russian security services. The Kremlin claims that Japan is using journalists as spies.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russia's attacks on Ukraine's capital, Kyiv, are intensifying. DW asked people on the ground what life is like</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65da070dc4667697603460c594e560bbe035ba9a41cce53a704f90d352e25378</id><updated>2026-10-25T19:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T19:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-s-attacks-on-ukraine-s-capital-kyiv-are-intensifying-dw-asked-people-on-the-ground-what-life-/a-79741090--9d6ca1b7b337.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-s-attacks-on-ukraine-s-capital-kyiv-are-intensifying-dw-asked-people-on-the-ground-what-life-is-like/a-79741090?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's attacks on the Ukrainian capital are hitting harder and more frequently, making 2026 one of the long war's bloodiest years for Kyiv. DW asked people on the ground what life is like.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Afghan women could lose one of their last paths to a higher education</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c6db53c3f492f44455e1d76487d89d6763a50b1a0d296503f47b373d78829d6</id><updated>2026-10-25T19:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afghan-women-could-lose-one-of-their-last-paths-to-a-higher-education/a-79745173--2a76364e2679.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afghan-women-could-lose-one-of-their-last-paths-to-a-higher-education/a-79745173?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US has defunded one of the last universities giving Afghan women the chance to receive an education after the Taliban takeover in 2021. DW spoke with a student who says she's lost hope of ever earning a degree.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine tries to shut Moscow's airports with drone strikes on Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0649ef9cbee3f315b60bce72d67385321cdec2c16b0957d4bf4b5afbcb31a731</id><updated>2026-10-25T19:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-tries-to-shut-moscow-s-airports-with-drone-strikes-on-russia/a-79737469--16f9cb7db516.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-tries-to-shut-moscow-s-airports-with-drone-strikes-on-russia/a-79737469?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Repeated Ukrainian drone attacks are increasingly disrupting operations at Moscow's airports. The pounding is part of Ukraine's plan to shut down Russia's airpace.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
